%U A033323 3150044696,7994665480,20209319824,50942982080,127962421824,320687278680,801143366296,1997602076552
%N A033323 Number of n-step self-avoiding walks on the square lattice having exactly 2 pairs of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A033323 Previous name was: Configurations of linear chains for a square lattice. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 05 2026
%C A033323 From _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 03 2019: (Start)
%C A033323 In the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992), a(n), the n-th term of the current sequence, is C_{n,m} with m=2 (and d=2). Here, for a d-dimensional hypercubic lattice, C_{n,m} is "the number of configurations of an n-bond self-avoiding chain with m neighbor contacts."
%C A033323 The terms a(1)-a(11) appear in Table I (p. 1088) in the paper by Nemirovsky et al. (1992).
%C A033323 (End)
%C A033323 The terms a(12)-a(19) are obtained from Table B1 (pp. 4738-4739) of the published version of Bennett-Wood et al. (1998), corresponding to Table 4 (pp. 26-28) in Appendix B of the arXiv version. In the authors' notation, c_n(k) is the number of n-step self-avoiding walks with k contacts, and the table gives c_n(k)/4; hence a(n) = c_n(2) is four times the value tabulated for k=2. - _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 04 2019 [Clarified by _Carlo Corti_, Aug 05 2026]
%C A033323 Here a contact is a pair of nonconsecutive vertices of the walk that are adjacent in the square lattice. The same table also yields a(20)-a(29) by the preceding conversion. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 01 2026
%C A033323 The ancillary file sq_isaw_counts.ser accompanying Beaton, Guttmann, and Jensen (2020) contains the exact values c_{n,m}, the number of n-step self-avoiding walks on the square lattice with m nearest-neighbor contacts, for n <= 59. In this notation, a(n) = c_{n,2}. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 11 2026
%H A033323 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A033323/b033323.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..59</a>
%H A033323 N. R. Beaton, A. J. Guttmann, and I. Jensen, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.05852">Two-dimensional interacting self-avoiding walks: new estimates for critical temperatures and exponents</a>, arXiv:1911.05852 [cond-mat.stat-mech], 2020.
%H A033323 D. Bennett-Wood, I. G. Enting, D. S. Gaunt, A. J. Guttmann, J. L. Leask, A. L. Owczarek, and S. G. Whittington, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1088/0305-4470/31/20/010">Exact enumeration study of free energies of interacting polygons and walks in two dimensions</a>, J. Phys. A: Math. Gen. 31 (1998), 4725-4741.
%H A033323 D. Bennett-Wood, I. G. Enting, D. S. Gaunt, A. J. Guttmann, J. L. Leask, A. L. Owczarek, and S. G. Whittington, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9803359">Exact enumeration study of free energies of interacting polygons and walks in two dimensions</a>, arXiv:cond-mat/9803359 [cond-mat.stat-mech], 1998.
%H A033323 M. E. Fisher and B. J. Hiley, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1731729">Configuration and free energy of a polymer molecule with solvent interaction</a>, J. Chem. Phys., 34 (1961), 1253-1267.
%H A033323 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys., 67 (1992), 1083-1108; see Eq. 5 (p. 1090) and Eq. 7b (p. 1093).
%F A033323 a(n) = 8*p_{n,2}^{(2)} for n >= 1, in the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992). - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 11 2026
%e A033323 From _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 01 2026: (Start)
%e A033323 a(5) = 32 counts the following 4 walks plus their rotations and reflections. (S marks the start of the walk and X the end).
%e A033323     o---o---o    o---o   X    X---o---o   o---o---o
%e A033323     |       |    |   |   |            |   |       |
%e A033323     X   S---o    S   o---o    S---o---o   S   X---o
%e A033323 (End)
%Y A033323 Cf. A173380 (d=2, m=0), A033155 (d=2, m=1), A001411 (all square-lattice self-avoiding walks), A336492 (total number of contacts), A049230 (d=3, m=2), A046788 (d=4, m=2), A038728 (d=5, m=2).
%Y A033323 Cf. A038746 (p_{n,0}^{(2)}), A038747 (p_{n,1}^{(2)}).
